WEBVTT

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.410
It's been 3 months since the battle 
with the Skrugg was finished. 

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:51.920
Peace has returned to the city, but it's not 
like everything is the way it used to be. 

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:59.300
Deep scars remain from the Skrugg, and a 
large number of people lost their homes. 

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:05.280
Those spheres stopped moving, and 
have remained where they are. 

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:09.980
It doesn't seem like we have the technology 
on this planet to reactivate them. 

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.590
I heard on the news that the government

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:20.270
has finished surrounding the sphere in front 
of the White House with a research lab. 

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:26.720
The utilities and transportation networks 
haven't been fully restored yet, either. 

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.500
But... Even so... 

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.090
Okay, just hold it like that. 

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.570
Okay! No problem! 

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:36.050
Here I go! 

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.430
Ready, set... 

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:44.010
Everyone in the city is taking 
a new step toward tomorrow. 

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.320
And I've got a ton more work 
to do at my part-time job! 

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:53.190
Joey! I've got a lot of 
work again for you today! 

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.900
Right! Thank you! 

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.970
According to the latest reports,

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:08.160
the reconstruction of the areas destroyed 
by the spheres is proceeding as scheduled. 

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.870
And what of the investigation into the Skrugg? 

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:17.400
I am sorry, Sir, but although we 
are investigating quite diligently,

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:22.020
we still know nothing of the codenamed 
"Ghost" that destroyed the Skrugg. 

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.010
So, no change on that front. 

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:30.230
However, there have been small incidents 
in Center City during its reconstruction. 

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.910
Incidents? 

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:35.730
Well, I would hesitate to 
even call them that.... 

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:39.830
Overnight, piles of rubble have been cleaned up,

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.240
ground has been leveled,

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.280
scaffolding has been erected... 

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.620
It seems like someone is assisting 
with the rebuilding of the city. 

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.810
The work always seems to 
occur over a single night. 

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:57.810
And these are jobs that would take many 
weeks to finish even using heavy equipment. 

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:02.740
So you're saying that this "Mr. 
Hero" is hiding out in that city? 

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:11.350
We have no guarantee that this 
hero will always be on our side. 

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:18.100
Furthermore, if this mysterious hero 
and the Ghost are one in the same,

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:22.150
the United States cannot 
turn a blind eye to them. 

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.440
Do you have some evidence? 

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.800
This. 

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.250
It's a printout from a 
security camera in the city. 

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.120
That's... 

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:41.180
This Ghost may became a threat 
to the United States. 

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.600
Call Hughes. 

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.550
Let him handle this. 

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.130
You there, out of the way! 

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:11.120
You pitiful ants! 

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.490
Sheesh...

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:25.670
It is inadvisable to become 
overly emotional, Dr. Minami. 

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:26.950
I know that, damn it! 

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:33.190
Why do <i>I</i> have to help out here in Center City? 

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:37.520
Clearly because the Skrugg were destroyed 
prior to you stopping the sphere. 

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.510
I know that, damn it! 

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:47.360
Thanks to that, my beautiful work of art is 
being put to work rebuilding this puny city! 

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.530
Is there some other reason 
for involving the MR-1? 

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.820
Yes, of course there is! 

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.410
But I can't stand even watching it! 

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.440
Then perhaps you should not watch it? 

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.170
Of course not! 

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:04.050
You expect me to leave my work 
of art in other people's hands? 

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.090
Then you should watch it. 

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:11.430
I'm sure it's in this city somewhere... 

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.310
The one that got in the way 
of my grand ambition... 

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:18.810
It's in this city! 

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:23.970
What's the matter, Joey?  

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:25.440
Not getting enough sleep? 

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:26.870
Um, yeah... 

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:28.650
Sorry... 

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:39.600
Where are you going to go, Will? 

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.980
I don't know. 

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:46.340
But I can't stay here any longer. 

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:51.130
I can't live in human society with this body. 

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.230
I can no longer be with you, Lina. 

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:55.640
That's... 

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.160
Stay back! 

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.850
Stay strong, Lina. 

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:10.200
Brother! 

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:17.990
I haven't seen him since. 

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:24.250
My mother said he's sure to return. 

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:29.190
And my dad seems to be 
trying to forget about him

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:31.620
by absorbing himself in 
the reconstruction work. 

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:48.060
Lina! 

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:50.240
Joey, good morning. 

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.740
Good morning. 

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.080
How've you been? 

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.610
Yeah... Okay, I guess. 

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:03.990
Is that so? 

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:07.660
So, Lina... 

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.710
I know a lot happened and all...  

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:13.010
But keep on working hard! 

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.920
If something's up, tell me anything. 

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:18.100
I'll be happy to lend an ear. 

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:20.100
Really? 

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.310
That's something I can handle. 

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:26.190
Just talking about things can 
make people feel better, right? 

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.810
Yeah... Thanks. 

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:38.450
Then, um... 

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.330
Would you... 

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.080
...go out on a date... 

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:49.340
What? 

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.250
Would you go out with... 

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.760
Joey, Lina! 

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:58.070
What's your problem? You'd better 
hurry or class will start. 

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.370
Oh, no! 

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:00.480
Gotta run! 

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.030
Using this distributive law,

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:20.770
you can take these products of polynomials
and turn them into a single polynomial. 

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:23.960
This is called the polynomial expansion. 

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:28.070
This is the opposite process from factorization,

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:29.020
When class is over, I'll 
ask him out, no excuses! 

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:34.480
which we studied previously, therefore you 
can use that process to check your work. 

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:33.300
If I ask him nice and quick before anyone 
interrupts, then it should go fine. 

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.180
That's all for today. 

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.380
Joey! 

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:43.600
Oh, Lina... 

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.930
Um, you see... 

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:46.980
I... 

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:50.980
Joey Jones! 

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.340
Yes? 

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:55.550
Would you come here for a bit? 

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:56.870
Okay... 

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.200
What's with this? 

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.750
That was amazing... 

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.680
I tried making it yesterday. 

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:19.380
H-Hey! 

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.580
What the heck is going on here! 

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.020
Did something happen? 

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:34.090
I have a feeling like I heard Lina's voice. 

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.030
Must be your imagination. 

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:48.030
I'm gonna ask him out, this time for sure!

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:50.460
Even if something gets in my way, I don't care. 

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:53.210
I've got to get him to promise, then... 

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:55.090
But... 

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.160
Joey! 

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:57.460
Hey, Lina. 

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:59.400
Um, I want to talk about something. 

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.180
It'll just take a second. Do you mind? 

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.600
What? Am I in the way? 

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.470
Yes. You are. 

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:08.000
W-What's with you? 

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.620
Whatever, just be quiet! 

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:11.770
F-Fine, I get it. 

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:13.900
Let's go, Joey. 

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.450
S-Sure... 

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.360
What time is it? 

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:21.250
Um... Three thirty. 

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:25.380
Sorry, Lina! I have to 
hurry to my part-time job! 

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:28.240
Don't worry. I'll run with you! 

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.250
B-But... 

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:31.830
I'm running with you! 

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:34.090
S-Sure... 

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.230
Then, let's go. 

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:38.120
Right. 

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:43.880
From Dad? 

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:45.320
Hello? 

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:46.940
No, I can't. 

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.220
I'm... 

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.100
Wait, really? 

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:50.810
But... 

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.460
Sorry, I'm in a hurry. 

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:54.560
Wait! 

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.060
No, I wasn't talking to you. 

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.510
What in the world is going on? 

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.150
Joey! 

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:27.790
Would you get me another cup of coffee? 

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:28.640
Sure! 

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:32.470
Could you fill me up as well? 

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:34.170
Sure, of course. 

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:37.870
Thanks. 

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:38.770
No problem. 

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.980
Not bad. The coffee here is top notch. 

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:49.750
Yeah! Best instant coffee you can buy! 

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:50.370
What's that? 

00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:52.730
If you can't taste the difference, 
get outta my store. 

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.990
Sorry, sorry... Fill 'er up. 

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:00.620
Are you also here to help with the reconstruction? 

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.250
Well, something like that. 

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:07.840
The city needs a lot of workers to help 
with the rebuilding and construction. 

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:10.470
And thanks to that, I've got a lot more work. 

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.150
I see. Good for you. 

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:13.110
Yes. 

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:14.500
By the way, uh... 

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:15.230
Joey. 

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.720
Okay then, Joey. 

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:20.310
Have you heard the rumors? 

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:21.410
What rumors? 

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:24.730
That there's some hero that shows up

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:28.110
and helps with the reconstruction in 
the middle of night, uncalled for. 

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:30.760
You know about it? 

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.210
N-No! I... 

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:37.120
Well, maybe it's just some urban legend. 

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:40.630
You're investigating those rumors? 

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:46.510
No. Just wondering what you 
thought of someone that kind. 

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.870
I think it's the work of God. 

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.300
It's been a giant help. 

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:53.510
What are you talking about? I 
won't have any work left to do! 

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:00.730
I guess I should cut back 
on anything too flashy... 

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:09.260
Ready? 

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:10.700
Yeah! 

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.960
Then ready... Start! 

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:19.240
Heroman... Go! 

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:41.690
Heroman...

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:44.110
Attack! 

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:48.530
Okay! 

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.180
That's enough! 

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:52.030
Perfect. 

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.650
Professor, what's this? 

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:04.080
Heroman's power comes from electricity. 

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:10.040
Electricity is the origin of magnetism, and 
has the power to attract and repel things. 

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:16.740
I think you two have improved 
considerably these past three months. 

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.370
Plus your teamwork has 
made remarkable progress. 

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:21.490
You have some new attacks, too. 

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:26.110
Um, since the Skrugg are 
gone, why am I doing this? 

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:31.080
What are you saying? The Skrugg aren't 
the only threat to the world, you know. 

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:37.400
It's obvious that you must make all 
possible preparations for the next time. 

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:41.620
Studying construction is 
more useful to the city... 

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:46.460
Like how to pour concrete, or how to 
erect a steel frame foundation... 

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.360
Professor? 

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:59.850
Joey. You're the only one who can use Heroman. 

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:03.100
If you don't do it, who will? 

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:15.250
I don't want to see Heroman 
like that ever again... 

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:20.820
Yeah, that's right. 

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.790
Yup, and that's that. 

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:27.520
Um, Professor Denton... 

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:28.990
What is it? 

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:32.240
I heard that there are rumors about 
Heroman at my part-time job earlier. 

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:35.670
Oh, about the volunteer work 
you're doing at night? 

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:36.930
Yeah, well... 

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:44.020
Well, the rumors I've heard are that there are 
government types going around investigating. 

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:45.950
Well, don't worry. 

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:50.730
No one's ever going to think that your 
toy is some hero of justice or anything. 

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:56.760
That being said, I recommend that you 
take all precaution in your actions. 

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:58.760
Make up your mind. 

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:46.190
Sheesh... 

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:52.630
Who's that? 

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.280
Um, hello? 

00:17:58.280 --> 00:17:59.780
<i>Joey! It's Joey, right? </i>

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:01.110
Y-Yeah! 

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:03.810
Sorry about today. My job... 

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.180
<i>Anyway, where are you right now? </i>

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:08.010
<i>I have something I- </i>

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:11.740
Lina? Lina? 

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:12.980
What's the matter? 

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:15.280
Lina... 

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:20.280
Sheesh... 

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:37.050
That was... 

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.420
Lina! 

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.140
Quiet down, you! 

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:44.980
Sorry about this, little princess. 

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:47.680
You stay quiet and we won't 
have to get our hands dirty. 

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:50.070
For a little while, anyway... 

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.890
If you want to hate someone, hate your dad! 

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:58.570
We realized he must have been crazy rich after
he started doin' all that flashy charity work.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:02.290
It's obvious his daughter 
would be targeted, right? 

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:05.720
And that's that. 

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:08.930
As soon as your dad coughs up
the cash we'll go easy on you. 

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:10.830
Keep quiet until then. 

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.340
Who the hell are you? 

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:28.060
Joey! 

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.610
We got a strange one here... 

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:31.480
Move outta the way! 

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:35.190
Ignoring me? 

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.270
Fine by me! 

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:42.840
What the heck? 

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:44.460
Um, Boss... 

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:58.400
I-It's a monster! 

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.580
S-Stay back! 

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:07.500
Heroman...

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.850
Attack! 

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:21.290
Lina... Lina! 

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:26.780
It's okay now. 

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:30.060
Joey... 

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:32.050
Joey! 

00:20:32.050 --> 00:20:33.060
Lina! 

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:35.420
I was scared... 

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:41.590
But, I knew you would come for me... 

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:53.340
Thanks. Here is fine. 

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:55.250
Then, I'll be going. 

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.230
Right. 

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.510
Joey! 

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.780
Thanks for today. 

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:06.780
Good night, Lina. 

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:14.230
I forgot to ask him out on a date! 

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:24.140
Why can't I say it? 

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:26.060
It's such a simple thing... 

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:33.210
Would you like to go out somewhere 
together on Sunday, Joey? 

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:39.310
U-Um... You forgot... 

00:21:40.890 --> 00:21:45.790
And that's how we finally 
promised to go out on a date! 

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:49.820
What did we do? 

00:21:50.130 --> 00:21:51.600
We're the victims! 

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:53.200
We were attacked by a monster! 

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:54.600
Let me go! 

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.450
We didn't do anything wrong! 

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:58.880
We got you on illegal possession 
of firearms, at least! 

00:21:58.880 --> 00:21:59.960
Those aren't ours!

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:01.460
Give us a break! 

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:07.670
This is Special Agent Hughes. 

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:11.220
Reporting to the President. 

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:15.670
The Ghost... is real. 

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:24.090
<b>"Can you hear this voice?"</b>

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:31.560
<b>I've been calling that, always, from deep within my heart.</b>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:45.460
<b>Would you, all alone, let another lonely one be next to you?</b>

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:51.010
<b>Because together it's not lonely, it's twoly.</b>

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:56.140
<b>See, you're not alone any longer.</b>

00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:59.990
<b>Just because there's no one next to me</b>

00:22:59.990 --> 00:23:02.540
<b>doesn't mean that I'm lonely!</b>

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:07.740
<b>For someone to notice this pain</b>

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:13.270
<b>that heart must have surely cried.</b>

00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:16.650
<b>Right now, we'll crush to bits</b>

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:20.350
<b>the fortress of our limitless sadness!</b>

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:24.050
<b>I'll take you with me!</b>

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:27.730
<b>Got it? I'm running through at full power.</b>

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:31.470
<b>To where you're waiting, left behind</b>

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:34.640
<b>in the place of tears...</b>

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:39.770
<b>I believe in you, with burning passion!</b>

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:43.560
<b>Come to me!</b>

00:23:50.890 --> 00:23:52.630
On the next Heroman: 

00:23:52.630 --> 00:23:55.940
What is everyone out there most afraid of? 

00:23:55.940 --> 00:23:57.950
For me... For me... 

00:23:58.300 --> 00:24:01.750
Hughes's investigation is 
getting closer to the truth,  

00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:05.150
but Joey has bigger problems than that. 

00:24:05.150 --> 00:24:11.970
With the entrance of, in Joey's view, the 
greatest evil of all, Joey shudders and weeps in fear! 

00:24:12.350 --> 00:24:15.620
Next time on Heroman #11: Menace. 

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:18.940
Heroman... Attack!
